        "original_id": "a7e9d59a-e9cd-50ec-ae91-8245c6718e41",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sugata Marjit\n- Organizations: University of Calcutta, Centre for Studies in Social Sciences, Calcutta, Centre for Training & Research in Public Finance and Policy, Ministry of Finance, Government of India, Reserve Bank of India\n- Places: Kolkata, West Bengal, India\n- Roles: Vice Chancellor, Professor, Project Director\n\nFacts:\n- The University of Calcutta is a public state university in Kolkata, West Bengal, India, and it was established on 24 January 1857.\n- The University of Calcutta is informally known as Calcutta University or CU.\n- Sugata Marjit is the former Vice Chancellor of the University of Calcutta.\n- Sugata Marjit is the Reserve Bank of India Professor of Industrial Economics at the Centre for Studies in Social Sciences, Calcutta.\n- Sugata Marjit is the Project Director of the Centre for Training & Research in Public Finance and Policy.\n- The Centre for Training & Research in Public Finance and Policy is funded by the Ministry of Finance, Government of India.",
